---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for wealth management firms | Decisive';
const description =
  'A sale price is a multiple times earnings. We grow the earnings behind your AUM and make them believable to a buyer, in 14 days.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Loss Aversion',
    body: 'The large household or senior advisor you are most afraid to touch is often the concentration a buyer discounts hardest, and the one most likely to walk. Naming it early is worth real multiple.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Certainty Illusion',
    body: 'AUM that grew on market beta can feel like performance. A buyer separates the market from the practice. The growth that was never yours is the first thing they price out.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Status Quo',
    body: 'A fee schedule or cost nobody has revisited in years reads to a buyer as risk or as margin they can take. Either way it is value sitting on the table, priced back to you.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For wealth management and RIA firms</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">You can't sell a practice on numbers</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">a buyer can't trust.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        A sale price is a multiple times earnings. <span class="dollar">We work both numbers:</span> we grow the earnings behind your AUM, and we make them believable to a buyer. In a practice, the value hides in which clients and advisors actually carry it.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Scan</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing what a buyer would re-price, and what you could recover.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">What a buyer re-prices in a practice</span>
        <h2>The AUM is visible. What actually transfers is not.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A buyer of a wealth practice tests client and advisor concentration, the quality of recurring fee revenue, how much of the book is the founder, the split between fee and commission, and whether the relationships transfer. Every soft answer is a discount, and every one is also worth you can build before you go to market.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Accurate and ugly beats polished and untrustworthy. Buyers know the difference.
        </div>
        <p>
          The mess isn't negligence. Growth covered it, and the people producing the numbers were never paid to look. Everyone who touches your books closes the month. Nobody is making your company worth believing, and that is the job we do. The day a sale, a merger, or a succession comes into view, every soft number converts from a chronic annoyance into priced risk, and the clock starts.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          The trailing-twelve clock doesn't start until the numbers are true. Every month you wait moves the sale date a month.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps behind a growing book.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers the way a buyer will. Three of the six do the most damage in a wealth practice. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one two ways, what a buyer discounts and what you can recover, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the company worth believing.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>The mechanism reads the same across industries, because the traps do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Professional services, $30M revenue</span>
        <h4>A clean close is not a fast one, and neither tells a buyer where the cash is stuck.</h4>
        <p>
          Cash was trapped in a billing and close cadence nobody had revisited, and clean-looking reports masked the leak. We rebuilt the rhythm, pulled the working capital forward, and put margin on a weekly line of sight, the kind of report a buyer believes. A fee-based practice runs the same play.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Working capital recovered</span><span class="v accent">$380,000</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Close time</span><span class="v">22 to 3 days</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margin improvement</span><span class="v">~$50,000 / mo</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Sellable-Numbers Scan and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Scan promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you see your practice the way a buyer will, in dollars, on both sides of the equation. You leave with the re-price read, the worth read, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Scan</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
